    <briefdescription>
<para>Common base of the decorators presenting a small-strain gradient-enhanced material as a finite-strain one. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>BaseMaterialType</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>A concrete class derived from Marmot::Materials::MaterialGradientEnhancedHypoElastic&lt;n&gt;; the wrapper has the same number n of nonlocal variables.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
What the decorators share: they own the wrapped material, keep its state variables in the slot <computeroutput>materialstate</computeroutput> of their own layout, forward its density, nonlocal viscosity and micro-inertia, resolve state names they do not know themselves in the wrapped material, and hand it the nonlocal fields together with their increment. The finite-strain interface passes the TOTAL nonlocal fields, while the wrapped material wants the fields <bold>and their increment</bold>; the increment is formed against the value of the last call, which each decorator keeps in a slot of its own layout (<ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_materials_1_1_gradient_enhanced_hypo_elastic_wrapper_1a68e4208d1f8eeac416433d3d1a20a6f3" kindref="member">baseMaterialIncrement()</ref> below). The kinematics <ndash/> which strain increment the wrapped material is driven by, and which stress it returns <ndash/> is the derived class&apos; own: <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_materials_1_1_gradient_enhanced_hughes_winget_wrapper" kindref="compound">GradientEnhancedHughesWingetWrapper</ref> (an objective rate, for a material incremental in stress) and <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_materials_1_1_gradient_enhanced_corotational_wrapper" kindref="compound">GradientEnhancedCorotationalWrapper</ref> (the logarithmic strain in the frame of the polar rotation, for any material).</para>
<para>Each derived class builds its layout in its constructor: its own slots, a slot for the nonlocal fields of the last call, and baseMaterialSlot, of size baseMaterial-&gt;<ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_materials_1_1_material_gradient_enhanced_finite_strain_1ab3f4081e35502f156353c8af36843478" kindref="member">getNumberOfRequiredStateVars()</ref>. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
